            "subheading": "",
            "title": "Foundations of Nature-Based Clinical Work",
            "content": "<p>12-week course exploring the integration of nature-based interventions into trauma-informed clinical practice. Built around the intersection of ecological theory, nervous system science, and applied psychological work, the curriculum covers the conceptual foundations, clinical applications, and ethical considerations of nature-based therapy across populations and settings.</p><p>For licensed clinicians, advanced graduate students, and helping professionals seeking to develop a grounded, research-informed approach to nature-based clinical work. Foundations serves as the entry course for the forthcoming CFBL Institute certification in nature-based clinical practice.</p>",
